This repository holds two different kinds of work under two different terms:
software, which is open source, and content, which is not.

Read both sections. Section 1 grants nothing that Section 2 reserves, and
anything not clearly inside Section 1 falls under Section 2.

================================================================================
1. SOFTWARE - MIT License
================================================================================

Applies to the software that builds and runs this site, AS SOFTWARE: the source
code, build scripts, tests, CI and deployment configuration. In directory terms
that is `src/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `.github/`, `deploy/`, and the repository's
configuration files.

This grant covers the code. It does NOT cover the human-readable prose that
happens to be embedded in that code - the page copy inside `src/app/**/page.tsx`,
the work history in `src/lib/resume.ts`, and the biography and tagline in
`src/lib/site.ts` are writing, not software, and are reserved under Section 2.
Take the components, the layout, the build pipeline; not the words they render.

